§ `Labour hire licensing in Victoria: the worker's questions`

§§ `Am I a labour hire worker (ss 9, 11)`

@export Am I a worker for a labour hire provider under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 9, 11)? You are if a provider supplies you to others to work and must pay you; or recruits or places you with others who must pay you; or recruits you as an independent contractor for others and manages your contract. It does not matter whether you are the provider's employee, have a contract, or are an apprentice or trainee. The regulations can exclude some individuals.
GIVEN `how I am engaged` IS A `How the individuals are engaged` @desc How you are engaged: a provider supplies you to others to perform work and must pay you for it; a provider recruits or places you with others who must pay you; a provider recruits you as an independent contractor for others and manages your contract performance; or none of these
      `the regulations exclude me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude you (or the services you provide) from being a worker under the Act (answer no if unsure)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I a labour hire worker` MEANS `ss 9, 11 -- a worker for a provider` `how I am engaged` `the regulations exclude me`

§§ `Is the business that supplies me licensed (ss 7 to 10, 13, 46)`

@export Is the business that supplies or places me breaking the rule against providing labour hire services without a licence, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 7 to 10, 13)? A business that provides labour hire services must hold a licence in force; you can check the public Register of Licensed Labour Hire Providers. The maximum civil penalty is 800 penalty units for an individual and 3200 for a company.
GIVEN `the business is` IS A `Kind of business` @desc The business that supplies or places you: a business of providing recruitment or placement services; a business of providing contractor management services; another business; or no business
      `its arrangement with the host is mainly` IS A `Character of the arrangement` @desc What its arrangement with the business you work for (the host) is, wholly or principally: the supply of labour; recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the host; or something else
      `how I am engaged` IS A `How the individuals are engaged` @desc How you are engaged: a provider supplies you to others to perform work and must pay you for it; a provider recruits or places you with others who must pay you; a provider recruits you as an independent contractor for others and manages your contract performance; or none of these
      `it arranges my accommodation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business procures or provides your accommodation for some or all of the time you do the work
      `the regulations exclude it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude the business, its services, or you, from the Act (answer no if unsure)
      `the regulations exclude me as a worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the regulations exclude you (or the services you provide) from being a worker (answer no if unsure)
      `it holds a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the business holds a labour hire licence that is in force (for example, it is on the Register of Licensed Labour Hire Providers and not suspended)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the business that supplies me unlicensed` MEANS
    `s 13 -- providing labour hire services without a licence` (`ss 7 to 10 -- provides labour hire services` (`The arrangement` WITH
        `the kind of business` IS `the business is`
        `the character` IS `its arrangement with the host is mainly`
        `the engagement` IS `how I am engaged`
        `accommodation is procured or provided for the individuals` IS `it arranges my accommodation`
        -- The worker cannot state what the regulations deem to be labour hire; the fixed answer is no (NOTES.md).
        `the regulations take it to be labour hire services` IS FALSE
        `the regulations exclude the provider, services or individuals` IS `the regulations exclude it`
        `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers` IS `the regulations exclude me as a worker`)) (JUST `it holds a licence in force`)

@export Must my labour hire provider show me its licence when I ask, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (s 46)? Yes: a licence holder must produce its licence for inspection when a worker for a provider asks. Not doing so is an offence (up to 12 penalty units for an individual, 60 for a company).
GIVEN `I have asked` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have asked the provider to produce its licence for inspection
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must my provider show me its licence` MEANS
    `s 46 -- the licence must be produced` (IF `I have asked` THEN `a worker for a provider` ELSE `nobody has asked`)

§§ `Protection for using the Act (s 86) -- if something was done to you`

-- A situation the worker may not be in: the form can ask "Was something done to you because of the Act?" first.

@export Is it against Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 for someone to sack me, refuse to hire me, treat me badly or threaten me because I gave information or took part in a process under the Act (s 86)? No one may threaten or intimidate a person to stop them giving information, continuing a process or complying with the Act, or dismiss them, refuse them work or subject them to any detriment because they did. Both are civil penalty provisions.
GIVEN `what was done to me` IS A `What was done to me` @desc What was done: you were threatened or intimidated; you were refused employment, hire or engagement; you were dismissed, or your employment, hiring or engagement was terminated; you were subjected to another detriment; or nothing of that kind
      `why it was done` IS A `Why it was done` @desc Why: because of information under the Act you gave or intended to give, or to stop you giving it; because of a process under the Act you took part in or intended to, or to stop you continuing it; because of a requirement under the Act you complied with or intended to, or to stop you complying; or for another reason
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is what was done to me forbidden` MEANS `s 86 -- what was done is forbidden` `what was done to me` `why it was done`

@export What is the most the person who threatened me, or sacked or mistreated me, because I used the Act can be ordered to pay, in penalty units, under Victoria's Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (ss 86, 94)? 200 penalty units for an individual and 800 for a company, on the Authority's application. The dollar value of a penalty unit is set each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004.
GIVEN `it was a threat` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was a threat or intimidation (s 86(1)); answer no for a dismissal, refusal of work or other detriment (s 86(2))
      `they are a company` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the person who did it is a body corporate (answer no for an individual)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most they can be ordered to pay` MEANS
    `the maximum penalty units for` (IF `it was a threat` THEN `s 86(1) threats or intimidation` ELSE `s 86(2) dismissal or detriment`) `they are a company`
